1. What is eBPF?
Interview Answer

eBPF (Extended Berkeley Packet Filter) is a Linux kernel technology that allows programs to run safely inside the kernel without modifying kernel source code.

Traditional networking:

Plain Text
Packet
|
iptables
|
Routing
|
Application

With eBPF:

Plain Text
Packet
|
eBPF Program
|
Application
Why Cilium Uses eBPF
Faster packet processing
Better scalability
Lower latency
Kernel-level visibility
No huge iptables chains
Senior-Level Point

"Cilium attaches eBPF programs at networking hooks inside the Linux kernel and performs service lookup, load balancing, policy enforcement, and observability before packets traverse traditional iptables paths."

